  "body": "## \ud83c\udfaf Changes\n\nFix example and integration configs that break with the tool versions they install.\n\n- `integrations/react/next-15/package.json`: `pnpm run dev` fails with `error: unknown option '--webpack'`. The flag only exists in Next.js 16, where Turbopack became the default. Next.js 15 already uses webpack for `next dev`, so the script goes back to `next dev`.\n- `integrations/react/next-16/next.config.js`: remove the `eslint` option. Next.js 16 dropped it from the config schema and warns on every start (`Unrecognized key(s) in object: 'eslint'`). The examples already removed it in #11991.\n- `examples/preact/simple/tsconfig.json`: `include` was `**/*` with `allowJs` and `checkJs`, so after `pnpm run build` the `test:types` script also type-checked the bundled `dist/assets/*.js` and failed. Narrow `include` to `src`, `*.config.ts` and `*.config.js`, like the other Preact examples.\n\n## \u2705 Checklist\n\n- [x] I have followed the steps in the [Contributing guide](https://github.com/TanStack/query/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md).\n- [x] I have tested code changes locally with `pnpm run test:pr`, or these tests do not apply to this pull request.\n- [x] I have followed the [AI contribution policy](https://github.com/TanStack/query/blob/main/AI_POLICY.md) and fully understand the code in this pull request, including any code generated with AI assistance.\n\n## \ud83d\ude80 Release Impact\n\n- [ ] This change affects published code, and I have generated a [changeset](https://github.com/changesets/changesets/blob/main/docs/adding-a-changeset.md).\n- [x] This change is docs/CI/dev-only (no release).\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n<!-- coderabbit-ai-generated:v1 -->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **Chores**\n  * Updated the development command for the React integration with Next.js 15.\n  * Adjusted TypeScript checks for the Preact example to cover its app and configuration files.\n* **Bug Fixes**\n  * Next.js 16 builds no longer skip ESLint checks, so lint issues can now be reported during builds.\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n",
